---
description: Hackathon Master Repo architecture and frontend rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before substantial changes.
- Preserve the existing Next.js App Router boundaries.
- Prefer semantic HTML and CSS/Tailwind before JavaScript for layout and simple interactions.
- Use `components/ui/` for generic primitives, `components/` for product components, `components/motion/` for GSAP, `components/visualization/` for R3F, `store/` for small shared client state, and `lib/` for integrations/helpers.
- Keep client components at the smallest interactive boundary.
- Use Lenis only for app-level smooth scrolling; respect reduced motion and clean up.
- Use GSAP + `@gsap/react` for complex DOM animation; use `useGSAP()`.
- Use R3F/Drei for Three.js scenes and lazy-load heavy WebGL.
- Use Zustand only when state is shared across distant client components.
- Reuse existing primitives before adding dependencies.
- Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` before declaring work complete.
